                reason — both are the same underlying data (raw-material
                stock moves tied to a manufacturing order), just viewed by
                product vs. by order, which the one pivot view already
                supports via its own group-by.
            Raw Material Orders is not built: it needs a purchasing data
            source, and the `purchase` module is not a dependency — real
            material ordering is part of ERP 10.8, deliberately deferred
            (docs/09-erp-integration-roadmap.md). Faking it with no real
            data behind it would be worse than leaving it out.
        -->
